# Plugins

Plugins are installed and activated via `scripts/seed-db.sh`. The list reflects
the choices made at scaffold time.

## Installed via seed-db.sh

| Plugin | Slug | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{{#if PLUGIN_CF7}}| Contact Form 7 | `contact-form-7` | Contact forms |
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_SUPER_CACHE}}| WP Super Cache | `wp-super-cache` | Page caching, HTTP/2 compatible |
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_RANK_MATH}}| Rank Math SEO | `seo-by-rank-math` | SEO, sitemaps, JSON-LD, OG/Twitter cards |
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_UPDRAFT}}| UpdraftPlus | `updraftplus` | Backups |
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_WORDFENCE}}| Wordfence | `wordfence` | Firewall, brute-force protection (deactivated locally) |
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_BSR}}| Better Search Replace | `better-search-replace` | DB URL swaps (staging → prod) |
{{/if}}{{#if MULTI_LANG}}| Polylang | `polylang` | Multi-language routing, hreflang, language switcher |
{{/if}}

## Configuration notes

{{#if MULTI_LANG}}- **Polylang** → Languages: add the locales configured at scaffold time
  ({{LOCALES_CSV}}), with **{{DEFAULT_LOCALE}}** as default. URL mode:
  "Directory" with no prefix on the default language.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_RANK_MATH}}- **Rank Math** → run the onboarding wizard. Local SEO settings produce
  schema.org markup; set address + phone to enable structured data globally.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_CF7}}- **Contact Form 7** → create one form with fields: name, email, phone,
  message. Note its ID and store it in a WP option for the theme to read:
  `wp option update {{PREFIX}}_cf7_contact_id <ID> --allow-root`.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_SUPER_CACHE}}- **WP Super Cache** → Advanced → enable caching → use expert mode
  (mod_rewrite). Exclude any pages with forms or live widgets from cache.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_WORDFENCE}}- **Wordfence** → set firewall to "Extended Protection" once site is public.
  Until staging is hardened, run in Learning Mode.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_UPDRAFT}}- **UpdraftPlus** → schedule weekly full backups to off-site storage. Keep
  last 7.
{{/if}}{{#if PLUGIN_BSR}}- **Better Search Replace** → used at production cutover, not part of
  regular dev.
{{/if}}

## Adding custom plugins

1. Create directory: `wp-content/plugins/{{PREFIX}}-custom-plugin-name/`
2. Whitelist in root `.gitignore`:
   ```
   !wp-content/plugins/{{PREFIX}}-custom-plugin-name/
   ```
3. Commit the plugin directory.
{{#if FTP_ENABLED}}4. Add the plugin slug to `FTP_CUSTOM_PLUGINS` in `.env.deploy.example` (and
   your local `.env.deploy`) so `./scripts/deploy-ftp.sh` mirrors it.
{{/if}}5. Add `wp plugin activate {{PREFIX}}-custom-plugin-name` to `scripts/seed-db.sh`.
